{"units": [{"id": "argeeis-note2", "translation": "where the word written in the codex, used by no one, ἀργίας [shining], with the letter r, which had been omitted at first, later inserted by the same, as it seems, hand, Blomfield correctly corrected by restoring the disyllabic form ἀργᾶς [shining], as Pindar said ταῦρον ἀργᾶντα [a shining bull] for ἀργάεντα [shining] in Olymp. 13, 99, and there are other examples of this kind of contraction, frequent in oblique cases, rare in the nominative. However, Blomfield should have written not ἀργᾶς [shining], but ἀργᾷς [shining] with iota subscript, about which Thiersch warned in the Commentaries of the Bavarian Academy vol. 7 p. 357: whence perhaps the codex reading ΑΡΓΙΑΣ [shining] is to be explained, which may have been put for ΑΡΓΑΙΣ [shining]."}, {"id": "argeeis-quote1", "translation": "the black one and the one behind, shining,"}, {"id": "argeeis-word1", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word2", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word3", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word4", "translation": "a shining bull"}, {"id": "argeeis-word5", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word6", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word7", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word8", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argeeis-word9", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "arges-orth1", "translation": "shining, white"}, {"id": "arges-def1", "translation": "shining, white"}, {"id": "arges-quote1", "translation": "with a white fleece"}, {"id": "argestes_persicum-orth1", "translation": "Argestes (a Persian proper name)"}, {"id": "argestes_persicum-def1", "translation": "a Persian proper name"}, {"id": "argestes_persicum-note1", "translation": "where it is contracted by crasis to καργηστήν [Argestes]."}, {"id": "argestes_persicum-word1", "translation": "Argestes"}, {"id": "argestes_candidus-orth1", "translation": "shining, white"}, {"id": "argestes_candidus-def1", "translation": "shining, white"}, {"id": "argestes_candidus-quote1", "translation": "white foam"}, {"id": "argestes_candidus-quote2", "translation": "a winged, shining serpent"}, {"id": "argias-orth1", "translation": "shining (erroneous for ἀργᾷς; see ἀργήεις)"}, {"id": "argias-note1", "translation": "[erroneous for ἀργᾷς [shining]. See ἀργήεις [shining].]"}, {"id": "argias-word1", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argias-word2", "translation": "shining"}, {"id": "argolis-orth1", "translation": "Argive (feminine)"}, {"id": "argolis-def1", "translation": "Argive (feminine)"}, {"id": "argolis-quote1", "translation": "For the clothing of the women is not Argive."}, {"id": "argos_filius-orth1", "translation": "Argus, son of Earth"}, {"id": "argos_filius-def1", "translation": "Argus, son of Earth"}, {"id": "argos_filius-quote1", "translation": "the phantom of earth-born Argus"}, {"id": "argos_filius-quote2", "translation": "and the earth-born herdsman, unyielding in anger, Argus"}, {"id": "argos_filius-quote3", "translation": "Argus, whom Hermes, the son of Earth, killed"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-orth1", "translation": "Argos, city of the Peloponnese"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-def1", "translation": "Argos, city of the Peloponnese"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote1", "translation": "she will not willingly go back to Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote2", "translation": "she will bear a royal race in Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote3", "translation": "and in Argos paying fair recompense"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote4", "translation": "the greatest teacher of evils to Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote5", "translation": "the establishment of many choruses in Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote6", "translation": "first to address Argos and the native gods with justice"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote7", "translation": "you go to Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote8", "translation": "he will dwell in his father's house in Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote9", "translation": "the land of Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-quote10", "translation": "to Argos"}, {"id": "argos_urbs-word1", "translation": "the (neuter article)"}, {"id": "argos_iners-orth1", "translation": "idle, lazy"}, {"id": "argos_iners-def1", "translation": "idle, lazy"}, {"id": "argos_iners-quote1", "translation": "for he is idle in shameful deeds, but loves not to be base"}, {"id": "argyreos-orth1", "translation": "silver, of silver"}, {"id": "argyreos-def1", "translation": "silver, of silver"}, {"id": "argyreos-quote1", "translation": "where are the gold-wrought and silver drinking-cups?"}, {"id": "argyrelatos-orth1", "translation": "wrought of silver, silver"}, {"id": "argyrelatos-def1", "translation": "wrought of silver, silver"}, {"id": "argyrelatos-quote1", "translation": "with silver-wrought horns"}, {"id": "argyros-orth1", "translation": "silver"}, {"id": "argyros-def1", "translation": "silver"}, {"id": "argyros-quote1", "translation": "there is a certain fountain of silver for them"}, {"id": "argyros-quote2", "translation": "the handle of silver"}, {"id": "argyrosteres-orth1", "translation": "depriving of money"}, {"id": "argyrosteres-note1", "translation": "[depriving of money]"}, {"id": "argyrosteres-note2", "translation": "in the verses of an interpolator"}, {"id": "argyrosteres-quote1", "translation": "and thinking of a life deprived of money"}, {"id": "argyrotoichos-orth1", "translation": "with silver walls"}, {"id": "argyrotoichos-def1", "translation": "with silver walls"}, {"id": "argyrotoichos-quote1", "translation": "of a silver-walled tub"}, {"id": "argyronetos-orth1", "translation": "bought with silver"}, {"id": "argyronetos-def1", "translation": "bought with silver"}, {"id": "argyronetos-quote1", "translation": "wealth and silver-bought fabrics"}, {"id": "argo-orth1", "translation": "Argo, the ship of Jason celebrated by poets"}, {"id": "argo-def1", "translation": "Argo, the ship of Jason celebrated by poets"}, {"id": "argo-def2", "translation": "Argo or the Rower was the title of a play by Aeschylus (fr. 17-19)."}, {"id": "argo-note1", "translation": "On which passage see under the word αυδήεις [speaking]."}, {"id": "argo-quote1", "translation": "Where is the sacred speaking timber of Argo?"}, {"id": "argo-word1", "translation": "under the word αυδήεις"}, {"id": "argo-word2", "translation": "Argo or the Rower"}, {"id": "ardeuo-orth1", "translation": "to irrigate, water"}, {"id": "ardeuo-def1", "translation": "to irrigate, water"}, {"id": "ardeuo-quote1", "translation": "as much land as the broad-flowing Nile irrigates"}, {"id": "arden-orth1", "translation": "swiftly, utterly"}, {"id": "arden-def1", "translation": "swiftly, utterly"}, {"id": "arden-quote1", "translation": "and may he hurl his body swiftly into dark Tartarus"}, {"id": "ardis-orth1", "translation": "goad, sting"}, {"id": "ardis-def1", "translation": "goad, sting"}, {"id": "ardis-quote1", "translation": "the sting of the gadfly, without fire, anoints me"}, {"id": "ardo-orth1", "translation": "to irrigate, water"}, {"id": "ardo-def1", "translation": "to irrigate, water"}, {"id": "ardo-quote1", "translation": "Spercheus irrigates the plain with kindly drink"}, {"id": "ardo-quote2", "translation": "where Asopus irrigates the plain with his streams"}, {"id": "areithysanos-orth1", "translation": "with a thyrsus of Ares (epithet of a warrior)"}]}